    "problem_statement": "SSHClient.close() raises AttributeError when called after transport is closed\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen calling `close()` on an SSHClient instance, an AttributeError is raised if the transport or agent has already been closed or set to None.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport paramiko\n\nclient = paramiko.SSHClient()\nclient.set_missing_host_key_policy(paramiko.AutoAddPolicy())\n\n# Connect to a server\nclient.connect('hostname', username='user', password='pass')\n\n# Close the client\nclient.close()\n\n# Calling close again raises AttributeError\nclient.close()  # This should not raise an error\n```\n\nThe error occurs because the code tries to call methods on `None` objects after they've been set to `None` in the close method.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nCalling `close()` multiple times should be safe and not raise any exceptions, similar to how file objects and other resources work in Python.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nAttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'close'\n```\n\nThis makes it difficult to use SSHClient in contexts where cleanup might be called multiple times, such as in finally blocks or context managers."
